Z||000000||BBBAD GT||03-15-2000||01:01 PM||||Welp, after two months of owning the 87 GT, I've run across my first problems. <P>*The speedometer decided to quit.<P>*The radio decided to quit (but the clock still worked, when the button was pushed).<P>*Car died slowing down, then a check engine light stayed on until I got home.<P><BR>This is too funny, because I'm pretty sure each one of them are independent of each other. <P>I think I might know the radio problem, I was tring to hook up a CD player to the radio, and to get its power, I spliced into the fuse box.  I think I spread out the connections too far, and its acting like the fuse isn't connected (but that doesn't explain why the clock still works, they might be on different fueses, but the clock and radio are the same unit).<P>The speedometer has me baffled, must be something wrong uder the dash or at the trans lead.<P>I haven't run the codes yet to see what the check engine light is for. It might be related to the fuse panel being a little wobblie when I was messing with it before. <P>Anybody have these problems (loose fuse panel? failing speedo? failing radio but clock working?)  Thanks for the input.<P>Good thing I haven't sold my other car yet.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||03-15-2000||01:19 PM||||Actually, the speedo/radio problems may be related...check the radio fuse and all the others while you're at it.<P>Also check the wire harness connector at the speed sensor as it may have come loose (if you're standing at the rear of the car facing forward, the speed sensor is on the front of the transaxle assembly towards the passenger side).<P>Connector can come loose and result in no speedo/odometer...I knocked mine loose changing the oil filter, so it can happen.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||03-15-2000||01:46 PM||||yes, i agree, the speedometer and radio thing <B>are</B> related.  i believe they do share the same fuse.  as for the clock, the radio is equiped with a constant hot, to keep the clock working and the memory in place, i believe that you will find that on all radios.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||03-15-2000||10:58 PM||||I looked at the fuse identification diagram, and yes, the radio and the cruise control share the same fuse.  Haven't checked the code yet, probably do that over the weekend (too damn busy with a one and three year old )  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for the help guys.<P>||||reg||1
